   "design": "At benches with a tablet, the technician enters observations once in a form linked to the test run, and photos taken on it attach to the same run. The test system saves its data files to the run record, instead of files being copied and renamed by hand. Test software produces the standard tables and charts from the run data and fills the report template. The technician writes observations and conclusions. Photographing, checking the report and reviewing with the engineer stay with the technician.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Observations were written on paper, retyped and charted by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Tablet forms linked to test runs and test software that produces reports.",
   "still_hard": "Tests on outside rigs with their own formats.",
   "human_edge": "Noticing a crack that the sensors did not record.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less retyping; observing stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "engineer",
